# RR2c-1 (critical_qualifier_receivers_bug; steps/qualifier-receivers-20261010.md), a located limit: a root merge with
# a typed operand is built natively but the walk has no step for it yet, and the root's retained graph is run in a
# WalkRoot row, so the translator refuses the statement where it stands; RR2d lifts it (the PRIM carries the operand).
# In a method the retained body stays native-only instead (unit_rr2_merge_op_typed_bare_walk).
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
R: merge(Model; (int: w 5))
int: code 7
if: R\v * 10 + R\w != 15
    code: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
